    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lovingly maintained by the same owner since new, this warm and inviting home is presented in excellent turnkey condition and occupies an enviable position at the very end of a quiet cul-de-sac, directly opposite an expansive open green.\n\nSet on a generous corner site, No. 38 enjoys approximately 4ft of side space to the front, widening to approximately 8ft towards the rear. This provides significant potential to extend to the side and rear while retaining a generously proportioned garden.There is further scope to convert the attic into additional living accommodation, with strong precedent for both extensions and attic conversions throughout the development (S.P.P.).\n\nThe accommodation has been thoughtfully enhanced over the years, offering an excellent balance of living and bedroom space. A warm and welcoming entrance hall leads to the generous bay-windowed living room, centred around an attractive feature fireplace. Double doors open through to the open-plan kitchen/diner, which forms the heart of the home and flows seamlessly into the bright sunroom overlooking the rear garden. A guest WC and useful understairs storage complete the ground floor.\n\nUpstairs, the home continues to impress with three well-proportioned and versatile bedrooms, complemented by excellent fitted storage. The principal bedroom enjoys a particularly peaceful setting, overlooking the rear garden and offering a wonderfully quiet ambience, together with its own ensuite. The remaining bedrooms are equally well placed, enjoying a tranquil outlook across the attractive green to the front, creating a pleasant sense of space and greenery. A beautifully maintained family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\n\nOutside is another standout feature of No. 38. The exceptionally private, east-facing rear garden is larger than many within the development and benefits from the property`s end-of-row position, allowing excellent natural light throughout the day. Mature screening, landscaped areas and gated side access create a secluded outdoor setting, while the generous proportions allow considerable potential to extend without compromising the garden.To the front, a large cobblelock driveway comfortably accommodates three cars.\n\nWoodstown Village is a mature and highly regarded development nestled at the foothills of the Dublin Mountains, offering an excellent balance of peaceful surroundings and everyday convenience. Woodstown and Knocklyon Shopping Centres, Lidl Ballycullen and Tesco White Pines are all within easy reach, together with an excellent choice of sporting and recreational amenities including Ballyboden St Enda`s, Marlay Park, St Enda`s Park and the Dublin Mountains.\n\nThe area is exceptionally well connected, with convenient access to the M50 and a choice of public transport services, including the 24-hour No. 15 bus route. Families are particularly well catered for with a wide selection of primary and secondary schools nearby, including St Colmcille`s, Firhouse Educate Together, Gaelscoil Chnoc Liamhna, Sancta Maria College and Coláiste Éanna."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 1.78m x 5.05m\nWelcoming entrance hall with timber flooring, understairs storage, decorative wall finishes and carpeted staircase rising to the first floor.\n\nLiving Room - 3.30m x 5.90m\nGenerously proportioned living room with timber flooring, feature fireplace with timber surround and cast-iron insert, attractive bay window to the front and double doors opening through to the kitchen/dining area.\n\nKitchen - 2.81m x 3.74m\nWell-appointed kitchen offering ample floor and eye-level storage, stone-effect worktops, tiled splashback, Belling oven and hob with overhead Turbo Air extractor, together with a pleasant outlook towards the rear garden.\n\nDining Area - 2.37m x 3.74m\nPositioned alongside the kitchen and finished with timber flooring, providing a generous dedicated dining space with access through to the sun room.\n\nSun Room - 2.77m x 3.83m\nA fantastic addition to the home, flooded with natural light through extensive glazing and a Velux rooflight. Timber flooring underfoot with direct access to and views over the private rear garden. Currently used as a home office, this versatile space would work equally well as a second reception, playroom or relaxation area.\n\nGuest WC - 0.79m x 1.59m\nConveniently positioned off the entrance hall with WC and WHB\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 2.07m x 2.61m\nCarpeted landing with timber balustrade, decorative wall finish and window providing natural light, with access to all three bedrooms, the family bathroom and hot press.\n\nPrimary Bedroom - 3.02m x 4.22m\nGenerous double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, finished with timber flooring and featuring an excellent range of fitted wardrobes, overhead storage, integrated bedside units and vanity storage. Access to the ensuite.\n\nEnsuite - 2.05m x 1.94m\nFully tiled ensuite comprising WC, WHB and enclosed shower with electric shower, complemented by mosaic-style feature tiling and a window providing natural light and ventilation.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.92m x 3.53m\nGenerous double bedroom overlooking the front, finished with timber flooring and benefiting from fitted wardrobe storage and decorative dado rail.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.30m x 2.68m\nThe smaller of the three bedrooms, overlooking the front and finished with timber flooring. Currently arranged as a home office, this versatile room is ideally suited as a single bedroom, nursery or dedicated workspace.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.06m x 1.98m\nFully tiled family bathroom comprising bath with handheld shower attachment, WC and WHB with vanity storage, large wall-mounted mirror and chrome heated towel rail. A window provides natural light and ventilation.\n\n\nFront\nGenerous cobblelock driveway comfortably accommodating three cars, with an enviable end-of-cul-de-sac position directly overlooking an expansive open green.\n\nRear\nExceptionally private, east-facing landscaped rear garden with mature screening and gated side access. Generous proportions offer excellent scope to extend to the side and rear (S.P.P.) while retaining a substantial garden.\n\nNotice\nThese particulars are issued by Mark Kelly & Associates (MKA) on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through us. They are provided in good faith for guidance only and do not form part of any offer or contract. MKA has not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, services or equipment, and purchasers must satisfy themselves as to their condition and working order. All descriptions, measurements, dimensions, maps, plans, photographs, condition, permissions, licences, access, prices, rents, outgoings and other information are approximate, for guidance only and may be subject to change without notice. Maps and plans are not to scale. Photographs are provided for presentation and guidance purposes. Where appropriate, AI-assisted enhancement, refinement or virtual furnishing may be used to improve presentation or assist purchasers in visualising layout, scale or potential. Such imagery is not intended to materially alter or misrepresent the structure, layout, condition or features of the property. Neither MKA nor its staff or representatives have authority to make or give any representation or warranty in relation to the property.\n"
      },
